1
00:00:13,888 --> 00:00:16,933
OUR STICKY LOVE

2
00:00:31,781 --> 00:00:33,824
The clumsy kiss…

3
00:00:33,825 --> 00:00:34,909
Forget it.

4
00:00:39,289 --> 00:00:40,457
This one's for real.

5
00:00:49,174 --> 00:00:53,928
I don't get why people say that even rags
can look designer on a great body.

6
00:00:54,596 --> 00:00:57,681
It takes hard work to get a great body.

7
00:00:57,682 --> 00:00:59,100
Why dress yourself in rags?

8
00:01:13,073 --> 00:01:14,365
DETECTIVE AGENCY

9
00:01:15,033 --> 00:01:17,367
- Yes?
<i>- We found a patient named Go Ji-won.</i>

10
00:01:17,368 --> 00:01:19,995
<i>In her early thirties.
Admitted two weeks ago.</i>

11
00:01:19,996 --> 00:01:22,039
<i>She's at a university hospital
in Gyeongbuk.</i>

12
00:01:22,040 --> 00:01:24,084
Are you sure the patient is Go Ji-won?

13
00:01:24,626 --> 00:01:26,461
Tell me the hospital's location.

14
00:02:02,288 --> 00:02:03,915
You go first.

15
00:02:10,839 --> 00:02:11,714
You stopped crying.

16
00:02:19,139 --> 00:02:22,058
You made me stop crying.

17
00:02:23,810 --> 00:02:24,644
Yeah.

18
00:02:27,397 --> 00:02:30,233
If that was your goal, you succeeded.

19
00:02:33,027 --> 00:02:34,404
That's a relief.

20
00:02:36,698 --> 00:02:38,825
That doesn't make it okay.

21
00:02:42,829 --> 00:02:47,332
Though I guess
I did the same thing yesterday.

22
00:02:47,333 --> 00:02:49,043
So I'll just call it even.

23
00:02:49,711 --> 00:02:51,336
Don't ever do that again.

24
00:02:51,337 --> 00:02:53,548
- Why not?
- Huh?

25
00:02:57,302 --> 00:02:59,846
What I meant to say was…

26
00:03:00,346 --> 00:03:05,392
When you've lived together for two years,
you're bound to bump lips all the time.

27
00:03:05,393 --> 00:03:10,147
When you've lived together for two years,
you do this all the time.

28
00:03:10,148 --> 00:03:13,650
<i>- Some days, it gets intense.
-</i> Some days, it gets pretty intense.

29
00:03:13,651 --> 00:03:15,444
<i>And some days, it won't end…</i>

30
00:03:15,445 --> 00:03:18,155
And some days,
it doesn't end with just this.

31
00:03:18,156 --> 00:03:20,950
You must be completely insane!

32
00:03:21,784 --> 00:03:25,079
You pretended to be such a gentleman,
but all men are the same.

33
00:03:25,914 --> 00:03:28,875
There's no chance,
so don't even dream about it.

34
00:03:32,003 --> 00:03:33,170
Let's go home.

35
00:03:33,171 --> 00:03:34,672
Excuse me?

36
00:03:35,173 --> 00:03:36,673
You want to take me home?

37
00:03:36,674 --> 00:03:37,967
Then will you live out here?

38
00:03:53,733 --> 00:03:54,567
Eat up.

39
00:03:55,944 --> 00:03:57,779
I heard you didn't eat much today.

40
00:04:06,371 --> 00:04:10,166
I guess you do know
a thing or two about me.

41
00:04:10,667 --> 00:04:11,584
Eat some rice too.

42
00:04:12,669 --> 00:04:14,629
You need a balanced diet
to recover quickly.

43
00:04:15,672 --> 00:04:17,339
Carbs make you gain weight.

44
00:04:17,340 --> 00:04:19,467
It doesn't matter. You'll still be pretty.

45
00:04:29,143 --> 00:04:29,978
This one's cooked.

46
00:04:36,109 --> 00:04:37,694
Aren't you going to eat?

47
00:04:38,945 --> 00:04:40,113
I'm full.

48
00:04:42,448 --> 00:04:43,865
Just eat.

49
00:04:43,866 --> 00:04:47,286
You think I'd be grateful if you said
you were full just watching me eat?

50
00:04:47,287 --> 00:04:48,620
but then have my leftovers?

51
00:04:48,621 --> 00:04:51,749
I really <i>am</i> full.
I had Chinese food earlier.

52
00:05:07,682 --> 00:05:08,516
What?

53
00:05:10,268 --> 00:05:11,644
It's just,

54
00:05:12,937 --> 00:05:14,731
I didn't know you could smile.

55
00:05:31,247 --> 00:05:33,207
I liked you from the moment I saw you.

56
00:05:38,296 --> 00:05:40,131
<i>This one's for real.</i>

57
00:05:45,011 --> 00:05:47,304
Why did he have to wear a suit today?

58
00:05:47,305 --> 00:05:50,183
I wouldn't have flinched
if he was in that scrappy boxer outfit.

59
00:05:51,351 --> 00:05:53,769
<i>I couldn't stop thinking about you.</i>

60
00:05:53,770 --> 00:05:55,104
I just hoped…

61
00:05:57,106 --> 00:05:58,483
to see you again someday.

62
00:05:59,692 --> 00:06:03,821
<i>Seeing you hurt was unbearable.
It killed me.</i>

63
00:06:04,781 --> 00:06:07,450
<i>You're the only woman I've ever liked,</i>

64
00:06:08,493 --> 00:06:10,745
so I don't really know how.

65
00:06:14,791 --> 00:06:17,210
If that look in his eyes was an act,

66
00:06:17,752 --> 00:06:19,462
then he deserves a best actor award.

67
00:06:21,631 --> 00:06:23,633
So he really is my boyfriend?

68
00:06:24,217 --> 00:06:28,178
Then what was that with the toad?
It didn't scare me at all.

69
00:06:28,179 --> 00:06:30,722
I guess you lost your fear
with your memory.

70
00:06:30,723 --> 00:06:34,227
The doctor said head injuries
can cause all sorts of aftereffects.

71
00:06:37,855 --> 00:06:39,732
Is that really it?

72
00:06:41,526 --> 00:06:42,902
Did I simply change?

73
00:06:45,029 --> 00:06:47,072
Oh my, Eun-sae?

74
00:06:47,073 --> 00:06:49,658
Go Eun-sae, what's wrong with you?

75
00:06:49,659 --> 00:06:53,036
If you can't wrap your head around it,
you don't have to.

76
00:06:53,037 --> 00:06:55,038
You don't have to believe it.

77
00:06:55,039 --> 00:06:59,127
Don't let those butterflies fool you.

78
00:07:11,597 --> 00:07:13,432
<i>Are you sure the patient is Go Ji-won?</i>

79
00:07:13,433 --> 00:07:15,268
Tell me the hospital's location.

80
00:07:17,854 --> 00:07:20,690
<i>He definitely said "patient"
and "hospital."</i>

81
00:07:21,983 --> 00:07:24,652
<i>The fact that he's scouring hospitals
to find Go Eun-sae</i>

82
00:07:25,528 --> 00:07:27,989
<i>means he thinks she's alive</i>

83
00:07:29,073 --> 00:07:31,200
<i>and doesn't know
Baek Sang-gil dealt with her.</i>

84
00:07:31,701 --> 00:07:33,327
She had these on her.

85
00:07:36,873 --> 00:07:38,458
That man is Mayor Ju's aide.

86
00:07:39,041 --> 00:07:42,127
He went undercover
to gather information on the prosecution.

87
00:07:42,128 --> 00:07:44,797
He's one of us,
so you don't have to worry about him.

88
00:07:48,801 --> 00:07:51,679
<i>The undercover agent is acting on his own.</i>

89
00:07:52,722 --> 00:07:54,265
<i>But why?</i>

90
00:07:55,433 --> 00:07:56,893
<i>How did he know to come here?</i>

91
00:08:01,939 --> 00:08:03,149
KAITO

92
00:08:04,609 --> 00:08:06,694
Hey. Any progress?

93
00:08:07,320 --> 00:08:09,238
We have the stowaway boat's
departure date.

94
00:08:09,739 --> 00:08:11,032
<i>Good work.</i>

95
00:08:11,532 --> 00:08:13,451
<i>Make sure the information doesn't leak.</i>

96
00:08:16,120 --> 00:08:17,872
HONG'S BOXING GYM

97
00:08:18,831 --> 00:08:20,248
What the hell?

98
00:08:20,249 --> 00:08:22,709
I thought he was a mole,
not her real boyfriend.

99
00:08:22,710 --> 00:08:25,003
Why would he be looking for Prosecutor Go?

100
00:08:25,004 --> 00:08:27,797
What's more important
is that he knows about Taffy Village.

101
00:08:27,798 --> 00:08:30,717
I thought this place was safe
and hard to track down, so how…

102
00:08:30,718 --> 00:08:31,552
Hold on.

103
00:08:32,261 --> 00:08:34,096
You said he's been searching hospitals?

104
00:08:34,680 --> 00:08:35,765
What does he look like?

105
00:08:46,317 --> 00:08:49,152
That's him. This guy came here yesterday.

106
00:08:49,153 --> 00:08:50,070
What?

107
00:08:50,071 --> 00:08:53,532
- Are you the head coach here?
<i>- He asked if I was the head coach.</i>

108
00:08:53,533 --> 00:08:56,117
Did you happen to visit
a hospital yesterday?

109
00:08:56,118 --> 00:08:58,246
Then asked if I'd visited the hospital.

110
00:09:01,290 --> 00:09:02,124
You know,

111
00:09:02,875 --> 00:09:05,211
since he's managed to track her here,

112
00:09:06,045 --> 00:09:09,131
how about telling Prosecutor Go the truth?

113
00:09:14,136 --> 00:09:15,471
I slept like a baby.

114
00:09:21,394 --> 00:09:22,728
My gosh! Why did I sleep in so late?

115
00:09:24,814 --> 00:09:27,525
What's up with you, Eun-sae?

116
00:09:28,276 --> 00:09:31,278
You shouldn't be sleeping
so soundly already.

117
00:09:31,279 --> 00:09:37,451
You should still be suspicious
that all of this might not be true.

118
00:09:39,412 --> 00:09:43,416
We can't just wait around forever
for her memory to come back.

119
00:09:44,292 --> 00:09:46,167
She's suspicious anyway.

120
00:09:46,168 --> 00:09:48,503
Let's just tell her everything.

121
00:09:48,504 --> 00:09:51,006
Tell her that Baek Sang-gil
is no ordinary guy,

122
00:09:51,007 --> 00:09:54,218
so if she wants to stay alive,
she should leave Korea right away.

123
00:09:55,261 --> 00:09:56,762
Let's persuade her like that.

124
00:09:57,763 --> 00:09:58,680
We can't.

125
00:09:58,681 --> 00:09:59,681
Why not?

126
00:09:59,682 --> 00:10:03,310
If she hears all that without her memory,
she'll try to verify it for herself.

127
00:10:03,311 --> 00:10:05,103
Whether she's really a prosecutor.

128
00:10:05,104 --> 00:10:07,607
Whether I'm lying.
She'd try to get to the bottom of it.

129
00:10:09,025 --> 00:10:10,525
She'd be in even more danger.

130
00:10:10,526 --> 00:10:13,945
We could just stop her from doing that.

131
00:10:13,946 --> 00:10:16,281
<i>If someone has no memory of being burned,</i>

132
00:10:16,282 --> 00:10:19,118
<i>no amount of warning
will make them fear fire.</i>

133
00:10:21,829 --> 00:10:24,373
They need to remember
how hot and scary fire is

134
00:10:25,291 --> 00:10:26,834
to know how to avoid it.

135
00:10:30,338 --> 00:10:31,422
Fair enough.

136
00:10:31,964 --> 00:10:34,174
She still doesn't believe you,

137
00:10:34,175 --> 00:10:37,636
so even if we tell her all this
and insist she has to leave Korea now,

138
00:10:37,637 --> 00:10:40,514
I doubt she'd just say "Okay,"
and agree to leave.

139
00:10:41,932 --> 00:10:43,058
Goodness.

140
00:10:43,059 --> 00:10:45,436
I guess we need her memory back fast.

141
00:10:46,520 --> 00:10:47,772
We're running out of time.

142
00:10:48,648 --> 00:10:52,067
Kaito called and told me
the stowaway boat leaves in a month.

143
00:10:52,068 --> 00:10:53,861
She needs her memory back before then.

144
00:10:54,445 --> 00:10:57,114
Don't we need to do something
about that mole boyfriend?

145
00:10:57,823 --> 00:11:01,702
He even knows about Taffy Village.
Shouldn't we at least distract him?

146
00:11:02,328 --> 00:11:06,039
Baek Sang-gil could keep him at bay
faster and more effectively.

147
00:11:06,040 --> 00:11:10,419
He'd also want to stop anyone
poking around to find Prosecutor Go.

148
00:11:11,712 --> 00:11:12,672
Do you have a plan?

149
00:11:20,596 --> 00:11:23,057
<i>Sending you the detective agency's number.</i>

150
00:11:26,185 --> 00:11:28,603
You were asked
to find someone recently, right?

151
00:11:28,604 --> 00:11:32,441
I'll give you a much easier job
and pay triple the agreed amount.

152
00:11:37,947 --> 00:11:39,739
How childish.

153
00:11:39,740 --> 00:11:41,366
What's with the apples?

154
00:11:41,367 --> 00:11:42,409
BREAKFAST, LUNCH, DINNER

155
00:11:42,410 --> 00:11:44,245
What am I, a kid? Ridiculous.

156
00:12:09,270 --> 00:12:11,647
What are you doing here
so bright and early?

157
00:12:13,149 --> 00:12:14,275
I just…

158
00:12:15,943 --> 00:12:16,902
The reading fee.

159
00:12:18,696 --> 00:12:19,779
Reading fee?

160
00:12:19,780 --> 00:12:21,157
About yesterday…

161
00:12:22,158 --> 00:12:23,451
I was wrong.

162
00:12:25,453 --> 00:12:28,329
It felt like you were insulting my spirit,

163
00:12:28,330 --> 00:12:31,750
and you were so rude and disrespectful,
so I just stood my ground.

164
00:12:31,751 --> 00:12:35,170
I'd rather not receive payment
from a customer who isn't satisfied.

165
00:12:35,171 --> 00:12:36,672
It just doesn't feel right.

166
00:12:39,633 --> 00:12:40,468
Well,

167
00:12:40,968 --> 00:12:43,011
you got there in the end.

168
00:12:43,012 --> 00:12:44,388
That's good.

169
00:12:47,016 --> 00:12:48,349
I'm saying this because

170
00:12:48,350 --> 00:12:52,896
I thought I'd be the bigger person,
even though I really can't stand you…

171
00:12:52,897 --> 00:12:55,441
Come on. Where's this going?

172
00:12:55,941 --> 00:12:56,776
I'm sorry.

173
00:12:59,570 --> 00:13:01,947
- What?
- I said I'm sorry.

174
00:13:02,823 --> 00:13:06,368
As an elder, I shouldn't be fighting
someone who's so much younger than me.

175
00:13:07,870 --> 00:13:09,079
I wasn't at my best.

176
00:13:16,170 --> 00:13:18,088
Well, I also…

177
00:13:22,510 --> 00:13:23,803
apologize for my behavior.

178
00:13:27,807 --> 00:13:29,849
Gosh, you even know how
to lower your head?

179
00:13:29,850 --> 00:13:32,268
When did I lower my head?

180
00:13:32,269 --> 00:13:35,021
Then what was that damn bow?
Or did your neck take over?

181
00:13:35,022 --> 00:13:39,442
"Damn"? Are you here to pick a fight
or apologize? Which is it?

182
00:13:39,443 --> 00:13:40,611
A mix of both. So what?

183
00:13:41,695 --> 00:13:45,281
Thanks for giving this back.
You can leave if that's all.

184
00:13:45,282 --> 00:13:48,994
Don't you worry.
I'll leave even if you beg me not to.

185
00:13:57,127 --> 00:13:58,170
Madam Shaman.

186
00:14:02,800 --> 00:14:06,302
I'm giving you this because I also thought
I'd be the bigger person,

187
00:14:06,303 --> 00:14:07,680
even though I can't stand you.

188
00:14:23,195 --> 00:14:25,197
Absolutely ridiculous.

189
00:14:27,449 --> 00:14:29,868
Well, I guess she <i>is</i> an elder.

190
00:14:29,869 --> 00:14:32,620
She looked like
she'd never back down yesterday.

191
00:14:32,621 --> 00:14:33,789
What's gotten into her?

192
00:14:40,921 --> 00:14:43,966
Hey, I apologized just now.

193
00:14:44,466 --> 00:14:48,178
I even gave back the fee because I felt
uneasy about accepting your money.

194
00:14:49,096 --> 00:14:52,766
I've been downing cups of ice-cold water,

195
00:14:53,350 --> 00:14:55,477
but I'm still fuming inside.

196
00:14:56,186 --> 00:14:58,479
Tae-ha, you should really reconsider.

197
00:14:58,480 --> 00:15:00,899
If you take in a woman like that
as your wife,

198
00:15:00,900 --> 00:15:03,527
your life could go up in smoke.

199
00:15:08,532 --> 00:15:10,742
- This should be enough.
- What are you doing?

200
00:15:10,743 --> 00:15:12,994
For the broken Bodhisattva statue.

201
00:15:12,995 --> 00:15:15,080
- How can you…
- Please accept it.

202
00:15:16,999 --> 00:15:17,917
I'm sorry.

203
00:15:21,128 --> 00:15:25,090
And please apologize to Eun-sae.

204
00:15:26,759 --> 00:15:29,844
Instead of bringing her here
to apologize to me,

205
00:15:29,845 --> 00:15:32,096
you want <i>me</i> to go
and apologize to that brat?

206
00:15:32,097 --> 00:15:34,391
I heard that you grabbed her hair.

207
00:15:35,267 --> 00:15:37,269
- But--
- That's assault.

208
00:15:38,187 --> 00:15:39,270
Well, that was--

209
00:15:39,271 --> 00:15:41,190
You frowned on my becoming a thug.

210
00:15:43,525 --> 00:15:46,195
You despise violence,
yet you resorted to it.

211
00:15:46,695 --> 00:15:49,031
So please apologize.

212
00:15:49,698 --> 00:15:53,117
What about her disrespecting her elders
without knowing her place?

213
00:15:53,118 --> 00:15:55,204
If you apologize first as her elder,

214
00:15:55,704 --> 00:15:56,955
she'll follow suit.

215
00:15:56,956 --> 00:16:01,043
Right, I'm sure
that brat would do just that.

216
00:16:01,543 --> 00:16:02,669
I'm certain she will.

217
00:16:02,670 --> 00:16:05,172
She's just not in her right mind
following the accident.

218
00:16:05,923 --> 00:16:07,048
She's a good person.

219
00:16:07,049 --> 00:16:10,009
Do you look at people with a blindfold on?

220
00:16:10,010 --> 00:16:12,513
How can you be
such a bad judge of character?

221
00:16:14,848 --> 00:16:15,849
I know that

222
00:16:16,934 --> 00:16:18,394
you're also a good person.

223
00:16:20,020 --> 00:16:20,896
What's that now?

224
00:16:22,731 --> 00:16:23,941
I still remember

225
00:16:24,441 --> 00:16:25,985
how you'd give me rice cakes

226
00:16:26,485 --> 00:16:29,238
whenever you ran into me
on my way home from school.

227
00:16:30,739 --> 00:16:34,451
And how you used to stuff my pockets
with boiled eggs,

228
00:16:34,952 --> 00:16:37,121
saying that athletes shouldn't go hungry.

229
00:16:37,705 --> 00:16:39,415
Thanks to you, I was a good athlete.

230
00:16:43,919 --> 00:16:44,795
Thank you.

231
00:16:45,921 --> 00:16:47,840
Why are you saying all that now?

232
00:16:48,549 --> 00:16:50,509
You're saying whatever for your girl.

233
00:16:55,264 --> 00:16:56,432
I'd really appreciate it.

234
00:17:00,769 --> 00:17:01,812
What about dinner?

235
00:17:03,230 --> 00:17:04,314
Have you eaten?

236
00:17:05,899 --> 00:17:08,360
I made some red bean rice cakes
last night.

237
00:17:09,028 --> 00:17:09,862
I'll pack some up.

238
00:17:24,293 --> 00:17:26,837
Since I have this,
I guess I could color it in.

239
00:17:37,598 --> 00:17:40,516
<i>Eat breakfast, done</i>

240
00:17:40,517 --> 00:17:43,186
<i>Eat dinner, done</i>

241
00:17:43,187 --> 00:17:46,565
<i>When I opened the window…</i>

242
00:17:51,737 --> 00:17:52,696
You're up.

243
00:17:53,280 --> 00:17:56,742
I've been up for a while.
It's not like the bed is comfortable.

244
00:18:01,830 --> 00:18:04,833
That shaman lady came by earlier.

245
00:18:06,043 --> 00:18:07,043
She did?

246
00:18:07,044 --> 00:18:08,837
She apologized and even paid me back.

247
00:18:10,005 --> 00:18:10,922
That's good.

248
00:18:10,923 --> 00:18:15,803
I guess I'm not the type
to be hated for long.

249
00:18:19,473 --> 00:18:20,724
If you're done eating, let's go.

250
00:18:21,725 --> 00:18:22,642
Where to?

251
00:18:22,643 --> 00:18:24,393
The clinic you went to yesterday.

252
00:18:24,394 --> 00:18:26,939
You need treatment
to get your memory back fast.

253
00:18:28,357 --> 00:18:29,191
Get ready.

254
00:18:33,737 --> 00:18:36,197
What was that? If this is all a lie,

255
00:18:36,198 --> 00:18:38,533
shouldn't he be hoping
I don't regain my memory?

256
00:18:38,534 --> 00:18:41,119
Then why is he so eager to help me
get my memory back?

257
00:18:41,120 --> 00:18:43,455
Is he really my boyfriend?

258
00:18:46,041 --> 00:18:48,501
Why don't you try selling stuff
on Instagram too?

259
00:18:48,502 --> 00:18:51,672
I bet you could get followers
and become an influencer in no time.

260
00:18:52,297 --> 00:18:53,298
No, I couldn't.

261
00:18:53,799 --> 00:18:55,383
Have you forgotten who you are?

262
00:18:55,384 --> 00:18:59,220
You're the legendary Min Su-ji
who ruled beauty forums back in the day.

263
00:18:59,221 --> 00:19:00,555
Right, Dr. An?

264
00:19:00,556 --> 00:19:02,266
Yeah, back in the day.

265
00:19:09,565 --> 00:19:11,608
I'm going to go brush my teeth.

266
00:19:21,243 --> 00:19:23,078
Hey, can we talk…

267
00:19:23,579 --> 00:19:25,247
How long will you keep this up?

268
00:19:27,457 --> 00:19:30,293
I told you that I had no choice
but to go on that blind date.

269
00:19:30,294 --> 00:19:32,713
I told you that my parents and I
run on give-and-take.

270
00:19:33,213 --> 00:19:37,550
They set up this clinic for me,
so I have to follow their wishes somewhat.

271
00:19:37,551 --> 00:19:40,470
I kept refusing until now,
and I only went on one date.

272
00:19:43,515 --> 00:19:44,516
Exactly.

273
00:19:45,017 --> 00:19:45,933
What?

274
00:19:45,934 --> 00:19:49,729
You kept refusing, but you never told them
that you have a girlfriend.

275
00:19:49,730 --> 00:19:50,646
That's because--

276
00:19:50,647 --> 00:19:53,567
At the clinic and with your parents,
you always hide me.

277
00:19:54,193 --> 00:19:57,695
You say it's because of what the staff
or your parents might say,

278
00:19:57,696 --> 00:19:58,988
but the truth is,

279
00:19:58,989 --> 00:20:01,199
I'm just not good enough for you, am I?

280
00:20:01,200 --> 00:20:03,784
- How could you say--
- Not some nurse's aide.

281
00:20:03,785 --> 00:20:07,080
You want to meet a woman
fit for a clinic director, don't you?

282
00:20:11,126 --> 00:20:12,668
Then what about you?

283
00:20:12,669 --> 00:20:15,589
If you felt that way,
why are you still with me?

284
00:20:16,173 --> 00:20:18,217
It's because I own a clinic, isn't it?

285
00:20:22,971 --> 00:20:26,225
- So I've decided to know my place.
- What's that supposed to mean?

286
00:20:27,476 --> 00:20:30,853
I'm saying we should break up.
You're free to go on those blind dates.

287
00:20:30,854 --> 00:20:32,898
I'll find a man who's more on my level.

288
00:20:34,233 --> 00:20:35,234
Hey, Min Su-ji.

289
00:20:36,860 --> 00:20:38,195
- Su-ji.
- Hello.

290
00:20:40,113 --> 00:20:41,614
This is the director.

291
00:20:41,615 --> 00:20:44,451
Here. I brought him.
Someone to vouch for my identity.

292
00:20:45,994 --> 00:20:47,246
Nice to meet you.

293
00:20:47,746 --> 00:20:49,373
What's with the "nice to meet you"?

294
00:20:50,290 --> 00:20:53,085
- He said you were classmates.
- Classmates?

295
00:20:54,211 --> 00:20:56,255
Long time no see, Jang Tae-ha.

296
00:21:06,556 --> 00:21:08,808
All right, 1,000 won for a round!

297
00:21:08,809 --> 00:21:10,602
Come play balloon toss!

298
00:21:14,815 --> 00:21:17,817
- Wow, Min Su-ji is so pretty.
- No wonder she's Internet famous.

299
00:21:17,818 --> 00:21:20,236
Wow, she's a goddess.
The "it" girl of Gujin.

300
00:21:20,237 --> 00:21:21,697
She's glowing.

301
00:21:27,286 --> 00:21:31,164
AN GI-JUN

302
00:21:35,335 --> 00:21:37,504
Get your makeup done here!

303
00:21:38,505 --> 00:21:39,506
Here's your <i>yulmu</i> tea.

304
00:21:41,174 --> 00:21:44,553
Thanks. I just love <i>yulmu</i> tea.

305
00:21:51,560 --> 00:21:52,853
It's boiling today.

306
00:21:55,272 --> 00:21:56,856
Should we get drinks? Cola?

307
00:21:56,857 --> 00:21:58,524
- Cola sounds good.
- Sure.

308
00:21:58,525 --> 00:22:01,027
Hey, can we get three colas?

309
00:22:01,028 --> 00:22:02,195
Sure.

310
00:22:19,379 --> 00:22:21,173
Wipe your sweat with this.

311
00:22:22,507 --> 00:22:23,342
Thanks.

312
00:22:27,304 --> 00:22:28,889
What was your name again?

313
00:22:30,057 --> 00:22:31,808
Su… Sun-deok?

314
00:22:32,768 --> 00:22:35,145
That would be me.

315
00:22:36,480 --> 00:22:38,898
It's Su-ji. Min Su-ji.

316
00:22:38,899 --> 00:22:40,650
Of course. Thanks, Min Su-ji.

317
00:23:04,591 --> 00:23:06,258
DIRECTOR AN GI-JUN

318
00:23:06,259 --> 00:23:07,719
Oh, come on.

319
00:23:10,097 --> 00:23:11,722
Our nurses are so clumsy.

320
00:23:11,723 --> 00:23:13,015
Can I take a card?

321
00:23:13,016 --> 00:23:14,434
Sure, please do.

322
00:23:17,312 --> 00:23:19,523
Looking at this, I think I remember.

323
00:23:20,232 --> 00:23:22,609
Weren't you the guy
who always got the best grades?

324
00:23:23,902 --> 00:23:25,403
Well, not always.

325
00:23:25,404 --> 00:23:27,489
You were so smart,
and now you're a doctor.

326
00:23:28,115 --> 00:23:30,324
And how are you doing these days?

327
00:23:30,325 --> 00:23:33,494
I heard you got into something else
after you gave up boxing.

328
00:23:33,495 --> 00:23:34,788
I left that job recently.

329
00:23:36,081 --> 00:23:37,332
I see.

330
00:23:38,542 --> 00:23:40,709
Ms. Go Eun-sae told me
about her situation.

331
00:23:40,710 --> 00:23:43,003
But our hospital has regulations.

332
00:23:43,004 --> 00:23:45,048
- If a person's unverified, we can't--
- Thanks.

333
00:23:46,508 --> 00:23:47,843
You'll treat her, won't you?

334
00:23:48,927 --> 00:23:50,137
Otherwise, you wouldn't have called.

335
00:23:51,179 --> 00:23:52,973
Right, yeah.

336
00:23:53,932 --> 00:23:57,769
I'll pay whatever it costs,
so please do what you can for her.

337
00:23:58,395 --> 00:23:59,396
Okay.

338
00:24:00,063 --> 00:24:03,233
- It's a good thing I'm the director--
- Exactly.

339
00:24:05,110 --> 00:24:08,155
So these are the perks
of having a capable classmate.

340
00:24:09,865 --> 00:24:10,740
Thanks in advance.

341
00:24:12,117 --> 00:24:13,243
Yeah, sure.

342
00:24:17,747 --> 00:24:19,916
What are they talking about for so long?

343
00:24:21,877 --> 00:24:22,836
You're beautiful.

344
00:24:24,212 --> 00:24:26,464
Do you have a boyfriend?

345
00:24:26,465 --> 00:24:27,423
I'm sorry, but…

346
00:24:27,424 --> 00:24:29,258
I do. I'm sorry.

347
00:24:29,259 --> 00:24:31,470
Understood. My apologies.

348
00:24:37,976 --> 00:24:38,977
Here you go.

349
00:24:39,895 --> 00:24:41,187
It's okay.

350
00:24:41,188 --> 00:24:43,690
I only drink coffee
that's been freshly roasted.

351
00:25:09,883 --> 00:25:12,552
- How did it go?
- You'll come twice a week for treatment.

352
00:25:13,929 --> 00:25:14,763
Really?

353
00:25:15,680 --> 00:25:19,141
Ms. Go Eun-sae, we'll start with an EEG
and some basic tests today.

354
00:25:19,142 --> 00:25:20,268
Please come this way.

355
00:25:20,769 --> 00:25:21,603
Okay.

356
00:25:22,270 --> 00:25:24,439
- Good luck with the tests.
- Okay.

357
00:25:44,501 --> 00:25:47,504
If I'd known he was coming,
I would have put in an extra insole.

358
00:25:48,004 --> 00:25:50,090
Come on, Gi-jun.

359
00:25:51,216 --> 00:25:53,593
You always look so handsome,
but today of all days,

360
00:25:54,177 --> 00:25:55,929
why do you look so shabby?

361
00:26:14,406 --> 00:26:15,532
Hold up, An Gi-jun.

362
00:26:16,116 --> 00:26:17,200
Have some dignity.

363
00:26:19,160 --> 00:26:21,912
You have nothing to feel small about
anymore, okay?

364
00:26:21,913 --> 00:26:23,582
Jang Tae-ha is a former thug,

365
00:26:24,082 --> 00:26:25,292
and you're a doctor.

366
00:26:26,459 --> 00:26:28,627
You're on a different level, okay?

367
00:26:28,628 --> 00:26:31,714
If Su-ji has any sense,
she won't be interested in him anymore.

368
00:26:31,715 --> 00:26:34,759
Seriously, what is there to see in him?

369
00:26:37,804 --> 00:26:39,389
<i>It's been a while, Jang Tae-ha.</i>

370
00:26:45,395 --> 00:26:46,479
Don't you remember me?

371
00:26:47,063 --> 00:26:48,897
We were classmates in high school.

372
00:26:48,898 --> 00:26:50,525
Before you moved to Seoul.

373
00:26:51,234 --> 00:26:52,360
Right.

374
00:26:54,404 --> 00:26:55,572
Right!

375
00:26:57,616 --> 00:26:58,700
Su…

376
00:26:59,868 --> 00:27:00,702
Sun-deok?

377
00:27:03,580 --> 00:27:06,082
It's Su-ji. Min Su-ji.

378
00:27:06,791 --> 00:27:08,251
Right. Sorry.

379
00:27:14,549 --> 00:27:15,717
Are you back in Gujin?

380
00:27:16,843 --> 00:27:18,761
Yeah, I live in Taffy Village.

381
00:27:18,762 --> 00:27:19,887
With your girlfriend?

382
00:27:19,888 --> 00:27:20,889
Yeah.

383
00:27:29,272 --> 00:27:30,523
Hey, Go Eun-sae.

384
00:27:31,650 --> 00:27:32,566
Are you okay?

385
00:27:32,567 --> 00:27:34,985
I'm fine. I just stubbed my toe.

386
00:27:34,986 --> 00:27:37,781
- Does it hurt a lot? Can you walk?
- I'm fine.

387
00:27:38,281 --> 00:27:41,367
Stop overreacting.
People would think I lost a foot.

388
00:27:41,368 --> 00:27:43,161
- You should be more careful.
- Hold on.

389
00:27:50,460 --> 00:27:54,421
Once we have the results,
we'll start the treatment next week.

390
00:27:54,422 --> 00:27:58,175
We'll do a drug test, then begin
cognitive rehabilitation therapy.

391
00:27:58,176 --> 00:27:59,885
Thanks. I appreciate it.

392
00:27:59,886 --> 00:28:01,136
No need to thank me.

393
00:28:01,137 --> 00:28:02,055
God bless you.

394
00:28:07,143 --> 00:28:08,227
We'll get going, then.

395
00:28:08,228 --> 00:28:09,646
- Okay.
- Bye, Ji-su.

396
00:28:10,230 --> 00:28:12,732
It's… Su-ji.

397
00:28:22,659 --> 00:28:24,452
You seem happy to see your first love.

398
00:28:25,120 --> 00:28:26,036
Yeah.

399
00:28:26,037 --> 00:28:29,165
It looks like Jang Tae-ha's still got it.

400
00:28:38,007 --> 00:28:41,093
That woman earlier.
She was your classmate?

401
00:28:41,094 --> 00:28:43,555
- Yeah.
- I see.

402
00:28:44,431 --> 00:28:47,016
Well, she was… a bit pretty.

403
00:28:49,477 --> 00:28:52,896
With today's beauty techniques,

404
00:28:52,897 --> 00:28:55,274
almost anyone can look like her
with a little effort.

405
00:28:55,275 --> 00:28:57,818
It's only because I'm wearing
these tacky clothes,

406
00:28:57,819 --> 00:28:59,988
but if <i>I</i> dressed up, I'd be a knockout.

407
00:29:01,156 --> 00:29:02,365
Should we go shopping?

408
00:29:03,533 --> 00:29:04,993
There's a mall in town.

409
00:29:20,258 --> 00:29:22,135
- What do you think?
- It's pretty.

410
00:29:26,139 --> 00:29:28,266
- How about this one?
- It's pretty.

411
00:29:32,187 --> 00:29:33,188
How about this?

412
00:29:38,026 --> 00:29:38,860
It's pretty.

413
00:29:40,820 --> 00:29:44,657
Stop saying "it's pretty"
without meaning it.

414
00:29:45,158 --> 00:29:46,743
I do mean it.

415
00:29:49,662 --> 00:29:51,289
You looked pretty in every single one.

416
00:30:06,137 --> 00:30:08,348
How can you say that so casually?

417
00:30:25,031 --> 00:30:26,074
It's true though.

418
00:30:32,956 --> 00:30:34,666
You already put a pink one in here.

419
00:30:35,583 --> 00:30:38,336
That was coral pink.
This one is bright pink.

420
00:30:39,295 --> 00:30:40,171
They're different?

421
00:30:41,172 --> 00:30:45,050
Of course they are.
No two shades are ever the same.

422
00:30:45,051 --> 00:30:46,553
You really are clueless.

423
00:30:49,347 --> 00:30:51,057
This one's moist. I like it.

424
00:30:51,641 --> 00:30:54,519
And the ingredients look good too.

425
00:30:57,230 --> 00:30:58,314
One of those.

426
00:31:01,651 --> 00:31:03,486
I think that's enough for makeup.

427
00:31:05,864 --> 00:31:07,073
You know…

428
00:31:09,659 --> 00:31:11,661
There's one last thing that I need.

429
00:31:24,757 --> 00:31:26,675
Now I feel like I can breathe.

430
00:31:26,676 --> 00:31:30,053
A modern person needs a phone, after all.

431
00:31:30,054 --> 00:31:32,974
It's a shame
that it's registered under your name,

432
00:31:33,892 --> 00:31:35,560
but I guess it can't be helped.

433
00:31:37,812 --> 00:31:39,313
You look happy.

434
00:31:39,314 --> 00:31:41,482
Yes, today isn't so bad.

435
00:31:42,150 --> 00:31:45,360
We agreed that I'd get treatment,
I got a phone,

436
00:31:45,361 --> 00:31:46,695
and I went shopping.

437
00:31:46,696 --> 00:31:48,990
That was such a stress reliever.

438
00:31:50,283 --> 00:31:52,242
Let's see.

439
00:31:52,243 --> 00:31:53,244
Huh?

440
00:31:54,454 --> 00:31:55,914
I only picked up one of these.

441
00:31:56,623 --> 00:31:58,416
Did you add the rest of them?

442
00:31:59,459 --> 00:32:01,294
Yeah, you said it was good.

443
00:32:04,213 --> 00:32:06,173
I can't believe you.

444
00:32:06,174 --> 00:32:08,176
You didn't have to be so thoughtful.

445
00:32:08,760 --> 00:32:10,719
I have a small face,

446
00:32:10,720 --> 00:32:14,056
so one cushion foundation
lasts me a long time.

447
00:32:14,057 --> 00:32:15,475
When will I use all this up?

448
00:32:17,352 --> 00:32:18,686
They're not for you.

449
00:32:19,938 --> 00:32:21,439
Then who are they for?

450
00:32:22,565 --> 00:32:23,566
I heard this is good.

451
00:32:24,192 --> 00:32:26,152
- One for each of you.
- What's this?

452
00:32:30,823 --> 00:32:36,287
If I use this,
I'll really look as pretty as a new bride.

453
00:32:36,788 --> 00:32:38,373
Right, honey?

454
00:32:39,040 --> 00:32:41,459
Of course.
You'll be the prettiest girl in town.

455
00:32:42,460 --> 00:32:43,962
Wait a minute.

456
00:32:46,047 --> 00:32:49,424
One second. That's not how you use it.

457
00:32:49,425 --> 00:32:50,842
I'll show you how to use it.

458
00:32:50,843 --> 00:32:53,596
You only need a slight dab.

459
00:32:54,263 --> 00:32:55,431
I'll put it on for you.

460
00:32:55,932 --> 00:33:00,061
Like this. Just tap like this, and then…

461
00:33:00,645 --> 00:33:03,898
Tap, tap.

462
00:33:04,857 --> 00:33:07,359
Tap gently.

463
00:33:07,360 --> 00:33:08,695
Just like this.

464
00:33:11,489 --> 00:33:14,367
Your face looks brighter
just from evening out your skin tone.

465
00:33:15,618 --> 00:33:16,828
Wait a minute.

466
00:33:20,623 --> 00:33:22,165
Goodness me.

467
00:33:22,166 --> 00:33:26,086
Why are there so many different
colored powders to put on your face?

468
00:33:26,087 --> 00:33:28,464
I think this will look good on you.
One second.

469
00:33:28,965 --> 00:33:30,048
- Here.
- More?

470
00:33:30,049 --> 00:33:32,051
Just a little more of this.

471
00:33:33,594 --> 00:33:34,761
Okay.

472
00:33:34,762 --> 00:33:36,096
Wow, that's pretty.

473
00:33:36,097 --> 00:33:38,140
- Let me see.
- You look so pretty.

474
00:33:38,141 --> 00:33:39,683
Good heavens!

475
00:33:39,684 --> 00:33:43,896
My face looks so rosy and healthy.

476
00:33:44,564 --> 00:33:45,939
Isn't that right?

477
00:33:45,940 --> 00:33:48,775
This looks good on you,
so I'll give it to you as a gift.

478
00:33:48,776 --> 00:33:50,193
Use it from now on.

479
00:33:50,194 --> 00:33:53,822
- And for you, Song-wol…
- How lovely.

480
00:33:53,823 --> 00:33:54,657
This one.

481
00:34:05,168 --> 00:34:06,002
Thanks for today.

482
00:34:07,295 --> 00:34:08,129
For what?

483
00:34:08,629 --> 00:34:09,714
For dolling Grandma up.

484
00:34:11,007 --> 00:34:13,342
I never knew she was so pretty.

485
00:34:13,926 --> 00:34:15,386
You really like your grandma.

486
00:34:17,388 --> 00:34:18,556
Because she's my grandma.

487
00:34:22,518 --> 00:34:24,352
- Hello, Coach.
- Hey, Pil-seung.

488
00:34:24,353 --> 00:34:26,772
- Are you training hard?
- Yes, I am.

489
00:34:26,773 --> 00:34:28,356
- Good.
- I'll be going now.

490
00:34:28,357 --> 00:34:29,275
See you.

491
00:34:32,278 --> 00:34:33,154
Who was that?

492
00:34:33,654 --> 00:34:35,739
Ms. Pang's son. He goes to our gym.

493
00:34:35,740 --> 00:34:37,574
Who's Ms. Pang?

494
00:34:37,575 --> 00:34:40,536
A woman who hangs out
with the shaman lady--

495
00:34:41,245 --> 00:34:44,457
You mean the S.E.S of Taffy Village?

496
00:34:45,124 --> 00:34:46,125
Their leader.

497
00:34:46,793 --> 00:34:48,419
That lady.

498
00:34:50,338 --> 00:34:53,716
Her son is handsome.
He doesn't take after his mom at all.

499
00:34:54,383 --> 00:34:57,886
Don't tell anyone in the village
that Pil-seung goes to our gym.

500
00:34:57,887 --> 00:34:58,721
It's a secret.

501
00:34:59,388 --> 00:35:01,432
Who would I talk to in this village?

502
00:35:02,100 --> 00:35:03,976
I don't have a single friend here.

503
00:35:04,560 --> 00:35:08,356
Speaking of friends, you really don't know
any of their numbers?

504
00:35:09,148 --> 00:35:12,735
Wasn't there anyone I would
meet often when we lived in Seoul?

505
00:35:13,903 --> 00:35:16,404
I don't know.
You didn't talk about your friends much.

506
00:35:16,405 --> 00:35:19,700
But I must have had at least one friend.

507
00:35:24,497 --> 00:35:28,000
Why aren't my friends looking for me?

508
00:35:37,927 --> 00:35:39,553
We're closed for the…

509
00:35:39,554 --> 00:35:40,638
Hello.

510
00:35:45,518 --> 00:35:47,019
- Here.
- Thank you.

511
00:35:49,689 --> 00:35:51,816
She didn't contact you either?

512
00:35:52,608 --> 00:35:56,278
She didn't.
The last time we went shopping together,

513
00:35:56,279 --> 00:35:59,364
Ji-won got a little upset with me
about something.

514
00:35:59,365 --> 00:36:03,161
At first, I thought she wasn't
reaching out because she was still mad.

515
00:36:04,245 --> 00:36:07,540
But even after that, I couldn't
get through to her by phone or by text.

516
00:36:08,457 --> 00:36:11,169
So I was planning
to report her missing tomorrow.

517
00:36:11,711 --> 00:36:15,506
She's not missing. She had applied
for a long-term leave of absence.

518
00:36:16,132 --> 00:36:18,008
- Long-term leave?
- Yes.

519
00:36:18,009 --> 00:36:20,344
I don't know what drove her to do that,

520
00:36:20,928 --> 00:36:24,515
but if you hear from Ji-won,
please let me know.

521
00:36:27,435 --> 00:36:28,811
Okay, I will.

522
00:36:40,448 --> 00:36:41,866
DETECTIVE AGENCY

523
00:36:43,075 --> 00:36:45,244
Yes, have you found Go Ji-won?

524
00:36:51,209 --> 00:36:52,292
Thank you.

525
00:36:52,293 --> 00:36:54,587
Why did you ask to meet
in a place like this?

526
00:36:55,588 --> 00:36:57,839
We're not close enough
to share a meal, are we?

527
00:36:57,840 --> 00:37:02,052
The longer I search,
the more I realize it's no ordinary task.

528
00:37:02,053 --> 00:37:04,054
We can't report her missing,

529
00:37:04,055 --> 00:37:06,306
and finding someone
through unofficial channels

530
00:37:06,307 --> 00:37:08,892
is a rather discreet and important task.

531
00:37:08,893 --> 00:37:11,561
This kind of thing
isn't a walk in the park.

532
00:37:11,562 --> 00:37:13,105
What is it you're trying to say?

533
00:37:13,856 --> 00:37:16,525
I'd like to renegotiate the down payment.

534
00:37:18,653 --> 00:37:22,989
So you called me out here
to ask for more money?

535
00:37:22,990 --> 00:37:27,161
For large-scale jobs,
we don't cut corners on formalities.

536
00:37:31,791 --> 00:37:33,793
So committed to formalities, aren't you?

537
00:37:55,231 --> 00:37:56,065
Yes.

538
00:37:57,316 --> 00:37:58,859
Thank you for your work.

539
00:38:01,028 --> 00:38:02,822
DETECTIVE AGENCY

540
00:38:24,468 --> 00:38:26,679
BREAKFAST, LUNCH, DINNER

541
00:38:29,473 --> 00:38:30,558
She took all her meds.

542
00:38:37,148 --> 00:38:40,233
Like this. Just tap like this, and then…

543
00:38:40,234 --> 00:38:41,736
There we go.

544
00:39:25,988 --> 00:39:29,408
I told you to lie low.
Look where that got you.

545
00:39:30,368 --> 00:39:33,537
She did me a favor by disappearing
voluntarily. Why try to find her?

546
00:39:36,165 --> 00:39:37,375
Still,

547
00:39:38,459 --> 00:39:41,712
why must you go this far…

548
00:39:48,010 --> 00:39:50,054
The best way to grow an apple tree…

549
00:39:55,518 --> 00:39:57,144
is to cut off the buds

550
00:39:58,229 --> 00:39:59,438
that are bothersome.

551
00:40:06,237 --> 00:40:08,656
"What if I let this one be?"

552
00:40:09,365 --> 00:40:13,452
"What if I let it grow a little
and then cut it off?"

553
00:40:14,120 --> 00:40:15,413
A moment's hesitation…

554
00:40:18,207 --> 00:40:19,834
could ruin your entire harvest.

555
00:40:23,587 --> 00:40:24,880
No, but…

556
00:40:26,966 --> 00:40:28,633
Wait, hold on.

557
00:40:28,634 --> 00:40:29,759
Wait.

558
00:40:29,760 --> 00:40:32,303
Please don't kill me. Wait, please.

559
00:40:32,304 --> 00:40:33,973
No, wait.

560
00:40:34,557 --> 00:40:35,723
Hold on.

561
00:40:35,724 --> 00:40:37,101
Please, no!

562
00:40:38,394 --> 00:40:39,979
There's more than just the watch!

563
00:40:40,813 --> 00:40:42,273
It's not just the watch.

564
00:40:45,734 --> 00:40:47,236
There's one more thing.

565
00:40:48,112 --> 00:40:51,698
Prosecutor Go said she had prepared
one more thing besides the watch.

566
00:40:51,699 --> 00:40:53,909
That's what I was looking for.

567
00:40:54,410 --> 00:40:59,122
If I'm alive, and if Ji-won…
I mean, if Prosecutor Go is alive,

568
00:40:59,123 --> 00:41:02,460
surely I could be of use to you later on?

569
00:41:07,673 --> 00:41:08,841
Please don't kill me.

570
00:41:35,743 --> 00:41:36,577
What is it?

571
00:41:40,998 --> 00:41:41,916
You put makeup on.

572
00:41:43,000 --> 00:41:45,628
I bought so much yesterday,
so I should use it.

573
00:41:46,420 --> 00:41:48,214
Don't go falling for me.

574
00:41:54,220 --> 00:41:55,471
As if I could help it.

575
00:42:03,395 --> 00:42:04,522
It's so good.

576
00:42:07,149 --> 00:42:08,359
Oh, right.

577
00:42:09,735 --> 00:42:11,028
Let's go to Seoul.

578
00:42:12,571 --> 00:42:14,489
We lived there longer than here.

579
00:42:14,490 --> 00:42:17,784
I might remember something
if we go back to where we lived.

580
00:42:17,785 --> 00:42:18,744
We can't do that.

581
00:42:20,329 --> 00:42:21,330
Why not?

582
00:42:23,040 --> 00:42:24,291
You're not

583
00:42:25,417 --> 00:42:27,336
fully recovered for a long trip like that.

584
00:42:28,921 --> 00:42:31,464
It's not like we'd be going
to the other side of the world.

585
00:42:31,465 --> 00:42:33,467
It's only a few hours away.

586
00:42:34,385 --> 00:42:36,387
We don't have many good memories in Seoul.

587
00:42:37,346 --> 00:42:39,390
It'll just make us feel bad.

588
00:42:40,015 --> 00:42:43,768
Good or bad,
I need to find whatever memories I can--

589
00:42:43,769 --> 00:42:44,728
How about a ride?

590
00:42:46,188 --> 00:42:48,649
- What?
- You liked riding scooters.

591
00:42:50,192 --> 00:42:51,109
I did?

592
00:42:51,110 --> 00:42:53,153
Whenever you were stressed,
you'd go riding.

593
00:42:54,655 --> 00:42:58,200
You should try it.
It might help you remember something.

594
00:43:02,413 --> 00:43:03,330
Scooters?

595
00:43:09,962 --> 00:43:13,591
Why does this feel so familiar?

596
00:43:17,136 --> 00:43:18,304
Okay, let's start slow--

597
00:43:19,930 --> 00:43:21,098
I know this.

598
00:43:21,599 --> 00:43:23,600
Yes, I know this!

599
00:43:23,601 --> 00:43:24,893
I know this, I do!

600
00:43:25,394 --> 00:43:26,645
- Hold on tight.
- Careful.

601
00:43:32,776 --> 00:43:34,361
I'm good at this.

602
00:43:36,447 --> 00:43:38,157
No way.

603
00:43:38,741 --> 00:43:40,576
This feels great!

604
00:44:11,023 --> 00:44:12,732
Are they filming an action movie?

605
00:44:12,733 --> 00:44:15,318
Why are they speeding around
the village on a scooter?

606
00:44:15,319 --> 00:44:18,613
Exactly. Why are they speeding
when no one's even chasing them?

607
00:44:18,614 --> 00:44:19,822
Leave them be.

608
00:44:19,823 --> 00:44:22,950
- They're still in the honeymoon phase.
- That's the honeymoon phase?

609
00:44:22,951 --> 00:44:26,496
When it looks like shenanigans
from the outside

610
00:44:26,497 --> 00:44:28,081
but makes perfect sense to them.

611
00:44:28,082 --> 00:44:29,374
That's dating for you.

612
00:44:29,375 --> 00:44:32,878
I wouldn't know. The last time
I felt love in the air was in a past life.

613
00:44:36,423 --> 00:44:38,758
Oh, enough with that.
Let's go do our hair.

614
00:44:38,759 --> 00:44:39,801
- Let's go.
- Let's.

615
00:44:39,802 --> 00:44:41,719
- Just one last drink.
- Yes.

616
00:44:41,720 --> 00:44:42,638
Cheers!

617
00:44:51,939 --> 00:44:52,940
Awesome!

618
00:44:54,441 --> 00:44:57,402
This is so cool.
Why am I so good at riding a scooter?

619
00:44:57,403 --> 00:44:59,112
You said you'd done courier work.

620
00:44:59,113 --> 00:44:59,947
I did?

621
00:45:01,031 --> 00:45:01,907
Remember anything?

622
00:45:05,619 --> 00:45:06,578
I don't.

623
00:45:07,162 --> 00:45:10,248
But I can tell
I was good at riding scooters.

624
00:45:10,249 --> 00:45:12,793
My body remembers.

625
00:45:13,836 --> 00:45:14,795
What else did I like?

626
00:45:15,379 --> 00:45:16,295
What?

627
00:45:16,296 --> 00:45:18,841
Tell me more. I want to keep finding out.

628
00:45:24,179 --> 00:45:25,305
Taking pictures.

629
00:45:26,140 --> 00:45:27,015
Pictures?

630
00:45:48,787 --> 00:45:50,414
How do I look?

631
00:45:52,916 --> 00:45:55,251
Come on, it looks like I'm planted there.

632
00:45:55,252 --> 00:45:58,922
What's with these proportions?
My legs look so short!

633
00:46:02,843 --> 00:46:04,051
Look closely.

634
00:46:04,052 --> 00:46:09,265
Take it so that my feet are one centimeter
above the bottom of the screen.

635
00:46:09,266 --> 00:46:11,602
That way, my legs will look longer.

636
00:46:14,354 --> 00:46:15,856
How do I know these details?

637
00:46:17,107 --> 00:46:19,026
I told you that you liked taking pictures.

638
00:46:23,322 --> 00:46:26,200
Anyway, take it again. One centimeter!

639
00:46:44,426 --> 00:46:48,471
Well, that's a new level of ridiculous.

640
00:46:48,472 --> 00:46:52,517
Will it kill her to look at the camera?

641
00:46:52,518 --> 00:46:55,228
She's dead set on avoiding the camera.

642
00:46:55,229 --> 00:46:58,189
When did he become
such a hopeless romantic?

643
00:46:58,190 --> 00:47:01,902
He'll do whatever his wife asks him to do.

644
00:47:03,111 --> 00:47:05,446
- Why do we even bother?
- Such an eyesore.

645
00:47:05,447 --> 00:47:06,281
Let's go.

646
00:47:13,121 --> 00:47:15,749
Some of these
might actually be worth keeping.

647
00:47:16,250 --> 00:47:18,751
But I really don't remember any of this.

648
00:47:18,752 --> 00:47:22,213
Seeing how at ease I was and how much fun
I had in front of the camera,

649
00:47:22,214 --> 00:47:24,216
I think I really liked this too.

650
00:47:25,008 --> 00:47:27,845
Did I use any social media by any chance?

651
00:47:29,596 --> 00:47:33,516
If I liked taking pictures so much,
I might have posted them somewhere.

652
00:47:33,517 --> 00:47:38,020
I've already searched for Go Eun-sae
on all the social media platforms,

653
00:47:38,021 --> 00:47:39,690
but I haven't found my account yet.

654
00:47:41,108 --> 00:47:42,818
I'm not sure. I don't think you did.

655
00:47:44,903 --> 00:47:46,280
What about my usual username?

656
00:47:48,115 --> 00:47:48,949
I don't know.

657
00:47:50,242 --> 00:47:53,244
See? This is the kind of thing
that makes me distrust you.

658
00:47:53,245 --> 00:47:55,789
How could you not know
your girlfriend's usual username?

659
00:47:59,418 --> 00:48:02,963
Even if you really are my boyfriend,
I'm disappointed.

660
00:48:03,672 --> 00:48:05,382
Why'd I date such an indifferent guy?

661
00:48:14,224 --> 00:48:18,352
We tried a lot of things,
but I still couldn't remember anything.

662
00:48:18,353 --> 00:48:19,813
It was totally unproductive.

663
00:48:22,774 --> 00:48:24,526
Speaking of productivity,

664
00:48:25,444 --> 00:48:27,361
why do you keep following me around?

665
00:48:27,362 --> 00:48:29,197
Aren't you going to the gym to work?

666
00:48:29,740 --> 00:48:32,867
This is a special situation,
so Mr. Hong understands.

667
00:48:32,868 --> 00:48:34,327
No way.

668
00:48:34,328 --> 00:48:37,789
You must be crazy!

669
00:48:38,290 --> 00:48:41,876
If you just hang around like this at home,
who's going to pay the bills?

670
00:48:41,877 --> 00:48:44,546
I can't exactly go out and work right now.

671
00:48:45,255 --> 00:48:47,341
How are you going to support me?

672
00:48:48,759 --> 00:48:50,927
Ask all the village ladies and see

673
00:48:50,928 --> 00:48:53,930
if any woman would be okay
with her perfectly healthy husband

674
00:48:53,931 --> 00:48:55,140
sitting around at home.

675
00:48:55,724 --> 00:48:56,641
I thought--

676
00:48:56,642 --> 00:48:59,894
There's nothing more for me
to be curious about or find unfamiliar

677
00:48:59,895 --> 00:49:02,064
in this tiny village.

678
00:49:02,856 --> 00:49:03,815
So go out

679
00:49:04,316 --> 00:49:05,150
and work.

680
00:49:06,985 --> 00:49:10,197
Men look their best when they're working.

681
00:49:13,033 --> 00:49:16,202
Later, I'm going to help Pil-seung
for a bit with his sparring.

682
00:49:16,203 --> 00:49:17,912
I won't let you go hungry.

683
00:49:17,913 --> 00:49:19,705
Were you even listening?

684
00:49:19,706 --> 00:49:22,501
You're going to go out for a bit
and then come back home?

685
00:49:24,795 --> 00:49:26,003
I'm so sick of this.

686
00:49:26,004 --> 00:49:27,631
Completely sick of this.

687
00:49:28,757 --> 00:49:30,467
How will we afford our beef?

688
00:49:32,135 --> 00:49:34,221
I want to eat beef.

689
00:49:40,310 --> 00:49:41,561
I'd better go make money.

690
00:49:54,157 --> 00:49:56,702
We heard about your date today.

691
00:49:57,285 --> 00:50:00,454
- What?
- The whole village knows.

692
00:50:00,455 --> 00:50:03,542
That the two of you were like a scene
from a romantic movie.

693
00:50:04,918 --> 00:50:08,714
We just rode a scooter for a bit
to see if it would jog her memory.

694
00:50:09,214 --> 00:50:11,841
- And we took some pictures.
- Right.

695
00:50:11,842 --> 00:50:14,802
We were thirsty,
so we bought some drinks. That's all.

696
00:50:14,803 --> 00:50:17,597
That's what we call a date, buddy.

697
00:50:19,349 --> 00:50:21,935
I heard you were lying flat on the ground

698
00:50:22,853 --> 00:50:24,479
just to take her picture!

699
00:50:26,481 --> 00:50:29,317
She kept saying they looked weird
and made me retake them.

700
00:50:29,985 --> 00:50:34,448
They all looked good and pretty to me.
She looked pretty no matter the shot.

701
00:50:36,241 --> 00:50:40,662
Even the pictures she deleted,
saying they looked bad, were pretty.

702
00:50:42,372 --> 00:50:43,373
She kept denying it.

703
00:50:49,046 --> 00:50:50,255
Tae-ha.

704
00:50:51,006 --> 00:50:51,840
Yes, sir?

705
00:50:53,508 --> 00:50:55,010
Sorry about everything.

706
00:50:56,511 --> 00:50:57,512
What?

707
00:50:58,513 --> 00:51:01,516
So this is what it feels like
to have a mirror held up to you.

708
00:51:09,107 --> 00:51:13,569
Why are you going to a PC café
three days in a row?

709
00:51:13,570 --> 00:51:14,487
He's adorable.

710
00:51:14,488 --> 00:51:17,990
What's going to become of you
if you keep playing computer games?

711
00:51:17,991 --> 00:51:19,742
Hey, Geum-hyang.

712
00:51:19,743 --> 00:51:23,788
The idea that video games ruin your life
is old news.

713
00:51:23,789 --> 00:51:26,750
These days, you can earn millions
playing computer games.

714
00:51:27,250 --> 00:51:30,420
If he's not good at studying,
it might be better to get into gaming.

715
00:51:31,713 --> 00:51:35,174
I'm fully supporting
Pil-seung's gaming career.

716
00:51:35,175 --> 00:51:37,718
You even have to support him?

717
00:51:37,719 --> 00:51:39,553
He's already given up on studying.

718
00:51:39,554 --> 00:51:42,641
It's admirable that he's working so hard
on something.

719
00:51:43,350 --> 00:51:45,560
As expected,
you're so open-minded, Hui-ja.

720
00:51:47,979 --> 00:51:52,775
My darling Jun-sik,
cute like the meaty part of a mackerel.

721
00:51:52,776 --> 00:51:54,235
Don't bother.

722
00:51:54,236 --> 00:51:56,195
This 10,000 won is for you.

723
00:51:56,196 --> 00:51:57,279
Thank you.

724
00:51:57,280 --> 00:52:00,157
And Pil-seung is at the PC café, right?

725
00:52:00,158 --> 00:52:03,244
Take this 10,000-won note to Pil-seung.

726
00:52:03,245 --> 00:52:04,995
Pil-seung isn't there.

727
00:52:04,996 --> 00:52:06,706
He's not? What do you mean?

728
00:52:07,374 --> 00:52:10,960
He always goes to the PC café after school
to play computer games.

729
00:52:10,961 --> 00:52:11,877
No, he doesn't.

730
00:52:11,878 --> 00:52:15,507
He wasn't there yesterday
or the day before.

731
00:52:18,135 --> 00:52:22,930
Then where does he go?

732
00:52:22,931 --> 00:52:23,973
Is anything fun on?

733
00:52:23,974 --> 00:52:27,017
<i>…the ceremony for the Irang-dong
development project</i>

734
00:52:27,018 --> 00:52:31,230
<i>was attended by Gangju City officials
and Mirae Eden Company representatives…</i>

735
00:52:31,231 --> 00:52:33,274
They both look so shady.

736
00:52:33,275 --> 00:52:35,944
Their faces really rub me the wrong way.

737
00:52:39,197 --> 00:52:40,489
TOP 3 OMAKASE RESTAURANTS IN SEOUL

738
00:52:40,490 --> 00:52:41,700
Goodness.

739
00:52:42,784 --> 00:52:46,037
What is that? It looks delicious.

740
00:52:46,538 --> 00:52:47,872
Wow.

741
00:52:47,873 --> 00:52:51,459
Look at how shiny the tuna is.
It's totally my thing.

742
00:52:51,960 --> 00:52:54,421
It'd be perfect
if I could eat there right now.

743
00:52:58,008 --> 00:53:00,135
The Cheongdam

744
00:53:01,344 --> 00:53:02,721
Class.

745
00:53:09,352 --> 00:53:11,228
The vibe is amazing.

746
00:53:11,229 --> 00:53:14,565
The people who get to eat here
are so lucky.

747
00:53:14,566 --> 00:53:16,943
I bet it'd be a great spot for photos.

748
00:53:28,663 --> 00:53:29,581
This is

749
00:53:30,248 --> 00:53:31,249
me.

750
00:53:37,380 --> 00:53:38,589
Bestie?

751
00:53:38,590 --> 00:53:39,965
A FEAST WITH MY BESTIE

752
00:53:39,966 --> 00:53:40,967
My friend?

753
00:53:45,096 --> 00:53:49,017
GO JI-WON, PARK HYO-JIN
FOUND A MEMORY WITH JI-WON

754
00:53:56,149 --> 00:53:57,524
It's me.

755
00:53:57,525 --> 00:53:59,236
Yes, this is me.

756
00:54:01,029 --> 00:54:02,072
It's me.

757
00:54:10,580 --> 00:54:14,209
But why does it say "Go Ji-won"
under my photo?

758
00:54:16,419 --> 00:54:19,714
Is my name… Go ji-won?

759
00:54:21,967 --> 00:54:23,009
Go Eun-sae.

760
00:55:33,913 --> 00:55:34,956
They're not here.

761
00:55:35,749 --> 00:55:37,083
They aren't here.

762
00:55:38,084 --> 00:55:41,713
The clothes, this bag, the ring.
Everything in these photos…

763
00:55:43,923 --> 00:55:45,592
None of it's here.

764
00:55:50,388 --> 00:55:52,349
You hated superficial things.

765
00:56:05,820 --> 00:56:06,821
It wasn't true.

766
00:56:08,198 --> 00:56:09,449
None of it was true.

767
00:56:53,701 --> 00:56:56,579
HONG'S BOXING GYM

768
00:57:04,712 --> 00:57:07,506
I can't believe you, Tae-ha. And Mr. Hong!

769
00:57:07,507 --> 00:57:10,676
As adults, how could you just
watch a kid lie and do nothing?

770
00:57:10,677 --> 00:57:13,387
Pil-seung really loves boxing.
And he's good at it.

771
00:57:13,388 --> 00:57:17,100
Save it! So what if he's good?
He'll just end up like you, a thug.

772
00:57:17,892 --> 00:57:20,436
You showed us that yourself.

773
00:57:20,437 --> 00:57:23,856
You even made the national team,
and you still ended up a gangster.

774
00:57:23,857 --> 00:57:26,776
You think I want to see
my son end up like that?

775
00:57:27,819 --> 00:57:28,778
<i>A gangster?</i>

776
00:57:30,572 --> 00:57:33,700
<i>Jang Tae-ha was a gangster?</i>

777
00:57:56,973 --> 00:57:58,641
OUR STICKY LOVE

778
00:58:45,271 --> 00:58:49,234
Subtitle translation by: Jimin Choi
